","historical_business_count":0},{"category":"Specialty Food","historical_business_count":0},{"category":"Candy Stores","historical_business_count":0}],"history":[{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"19wx431VQzIHTz3DcDy2pw","review_id":"LROScpChkN8eMx5vrQgCKQ","date":"2013-01-06T02:20:25","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9417770504951477,"text_excerpt":"On a culinary food tour, Leah's was our pralines stop. I tasted the pecan brittle and got a whole creole praline. I found them really interesting. Having never had a praline growing up in California, I expected it to be crunchy like brittle. Pecan pralines, I learned, are very delicate candies that are much creamier and have a softer mouth feel. I found them extremely sweet, but of course, very delicious when you got that perfect pecan bite. Really lovely small shop! Perfect for souvenirs."},{"business_id":"19wx431VQzIHTz3DcDy2pw","review_id":"gmk-BHpr0esGxaM0q73DYg","date":"2011-11-17T19:59:03","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.940194845199585,"text_excerpt":"I know there are a lot of players in the NOLA pralines market, but my vote goes to Leah's. Cute little store that smells amazing once you enter. While eying all the goodies we were offered sample tastes, which sold me to buy some. The pralines are wonderful, but I adored the pecan brittle it was just delicious."},{"business_id":"19wx431VQzIHTz3DcDy2pw","review_id":"YscQLLJwYofjXJaM2b3mPA","date":"2017-03-09T18:14:00","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.938022255897522,"text_excerpt":"Leah's pralines was amazing. I had been looking all over New Orleans during my visit there for Mardi Gras for fresh pralines. Prepackaged boxes were sold in every market or every gift shop but I wanted them to be fresh and have that homemade taste and feel. The sign outside Leahs was pretty old-school and the window decor drew me in, not to mention you could smell the pralines from outside. I walked in and the first thing I saw were rows of fresh packed pralines and a glass case filled with chocolate confections and more tasty treats. There was someone in the back with trays of freshly made pralines on one of those tall rolling bakers carts, wrapping and sealing them, this is when I knew ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"19wx431VQzIHTz3DcDy2pw","photo_id":"K3o6IGunjUFiU9Hq_VWXfA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/K3o6IGunjUFiU9Hq_VWXfA.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0}]},"notebook_case":null}
